  "details": "So, using multimodal methods of hand/controller tracking (you can check ALVRs newer methods of multimodal) say with the vision pro, quest pro, quest 2-3-3s, that allow you to forward both hand tracking and controller tracking information at the same time, the avatars hands use the \"hand tracked position\" while interactions (The controller position shown when calibrating, interacting with menus, etc.) use controller positions. \n\nThis means that when the hands are occluded, the avatars hands \"freak out,\" while still being able to interact with menus and other elements.",
